Z||000000||Kelvin Vivian||12-23-2001||05:19 AM||||Is this the steering rack going bad?<P>I hear a "pop" sometimes when turning my steering wheel... This is in my 87 SE.  Is it difficult to change a steering rack?  I heard that remanufactured steering racks from the Fiero store were pretty good.<P>How dangerous is it to drive with a bad steering rack?  Seems like one could lose control.  My Fiero feels a little squirly sometimes when driving straight...<P>TIA,<BR>KV||||reg||5
Z||000001||JetroGT||12-23-2001||07:47 AM||||I have the same noise. I just got new upper and lower control arms so it's not that. Probably tie rods or the rack.||||reg||1
Z||000002||JohnF||12-23-2001||08:00 AM||||You aren't very descriptive as to when, why, under what conditions, etc the "pop" occurs, but here is one diagnosis:<P>A "pop" when turning is "usually" directional (only happens when you turn one particular direction) and "usually" happens loudest when the brakes are applied at the same time a turning.  <P>If this is what you have, it is very likely a front wheel bearing has gone bad.  ||||reg||9
Z||000003||JetroGT||12-23-2001||08:13 AM||||It only happens when I'm backing out of a parking place or stoped and turning the wheel. It dosen't matter which way I turn the wheel either. And when I'm driving straight I can hear a rattle.<P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/NewSigt.jpg">   <BR>I work where all the missing paperclips go.||||reg||1
Z||000004||avengador1||12-23-2001||10:03 AM||||I would say it is the steering rack is going bad. I have the same problem when I turn the wheel all the way in any direction, when Im backing up. It happens when Im all the way to one direction and start to turn to the other direction. I feel a slight pop and then its alright. I took it to my neighbor, who owns his own Gas station/repair shop and had him look at it the last time I had the oil changed. He told me it was the rack that was going bad. I guess this will be another project for the spring. <P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Avendgador1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||David Bartlett||12-23-2001||11:47 AM||||I had a "pop" when I turned hard left for about a month before my lower right ball joint gave out.  <P>Fiero's come to a quick stop when one of the wheels comes in contact with the top of the inner fender.  <P>Good Luck.||||reg||1
Z||000006||4BanGinFun||12-23-2001||05:27 PM||||on my old 86 se the whole front end steering etc was shot all the bushings and balljoints where gone it poped and thunked really good get it looked at soon i would drive it much like that <P>------------------<BR>85 se 2m4 5spd white<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.stopstart.fsnet.co.uk/flags/canada.gif"> <BR>www.angelfire.com/super/camaro0/||||reg||1
